    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0515" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg501"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCulloch,
                        collector, to Mr. Glenn, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1820-01-11"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">January</hi> 11, 1820</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have directed a number of men, who have
                    declared themselves to be citizens of the United States, to be landed from the
                    South American brig Congressio de Venezuela, Richard Nivon, commander, who say
                    they were shipped by certain persons for the service of that country against
                    Spain, with whom we are at peace. They appear previously to have made oath,
                    before justices of the peace for this city, that they were severally foreigners;
                    but they now say that other men made oath for them; and they have enlisted under
                    this simulated proceedings, as above said. *They will be brought to your office
                    this afternoon, that you may take such testimony as you see needful, and
                    prosecute the men who enlisted thus feignedly. <seg type="margin"
                    >[136]</seg></p>
                <p>A paper containing the names of seamen and shippers, authenticated by the oath of
                    Captain Daniels and the certificate of Captain Webster, of the cutter, as well
                    as the magistrates’ certificate of the oaths taken by the sailors before them,
                    are all sent herewith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAS. H. McCULLOCH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elias Glenn,</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
